{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>For</b> — \"his face is covered with fat,\" as though he needs to make a mound upon his thigh to extract [something] from the fat. This is by way of parable: in the beginning the wicked man grows rich, but in the end, the opposite — as in \"the wicked sprout like grass,\" and in the end: \"he dwells in desolate cities.\" Others say: he chooses a place where there is no settlement, to isolate himself for evil, for they were poised [מעותדים] like those about to become heaps [גלים], as in \"a heap of stones,\" and likewise: \"heaps strive.\""], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:44.143329691Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}